      <h1>Building an accessible dialog 🚀</h1>
      <p>Grain UI's <code>&lt;Dialog&gt;</code> wraps the native <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> element, so focus trapping, Esc to close, and the top layer come from the browser. This guide builds a delete confirmation and covers the four things custom dialogs most often get wrong.</p>

      <h2 id="when">When to use a dialog<a class="hash-link" href="#when" aria-label="Direct link to When to use a dialog">​</a></h2>
      <p>A modal dialog interrupts. Use one only when the person must decide something before they continue, or when the task needs their full attention. If they can keep working around it, use a popover or an inline panel instead.</p>
      <p>Good fit: confirming a destructive action, a short form that blocks the next step, a session about to expire. Poor fit: announcements, onboarding tips, anything with a "Don't show again" checkbox.</p>

      <h2 id="usage">Basic usage<a class="hash-link" href="#usage" aria-label="Direct link to Basic usage">​</a></h2>
      <p>Compose the dialog from its parts. <code>Dialog.Title</code> and <code>Dialog.Description</code> wire up <code>aria-labelledby</code> and <code>aria-describedby</code> for you, so a screen reader announces both when the dialog opens.</p>
      <div class="codeblock"><pre><code><span class="k">import</span> &#123; Dialog, Button &#125; <span class="k">from</span> <span class="s">"@grain-ui/react"</span>;

<span class="k">export function</span> <span class="f">DeleteProject</span>(&#123; project, onDelete &#125;) &#123;
  <span class="k">return</span> (
    &lt;<span class="t">Dialog.Root</span>&gt;
      &lt;<span class="t">Dialog.Trigger</span> <span class="a">asChild</span>&gt;
        &lt;<span class="t">Button</span> <span class="a">variant</span>=<span class="s">"danger"</span>&gt;Delete &#123;project.name&#125;…&lt;/<span class="t">Button</span>&gt;
      &lt;/<span class="t">Dialog.Trigger</span>&gt;
      &lt;<span class="t">Dialog.Content</span> <span class="a">closeOnBackdrop</span>=&#123;<span class="k">false</span>&#125;&gt;
        &lt;<span class="t">Dialog.Title</span>&gt;Delete &#123;project.name&#125;?&lt;/<span class="t">Dialog.Title</span>&gt;
        &lt;<span class="t">Dialog.Description</span>&gt;
          This removes &#123;project.deployments&#125; deployments. It can't be undone.
        &lt;/<span class="t">Dialog.Description</span>&gt;
        &lt;<span class="t">Dialog.Close</span> <span class="a">asChild</span>&gt;
          &lt;<span class="t">Button</span>&gt;Cancel&lt;/<span class="t">Button</span>&gt;
        &lt;/<span class="t">Dialog.Close</span>&gt;
        &lt;<span class="t">Button</span> <span class="a">variant</span>=<span class="s">"danger"</span> <span class="a">onClick</span>=&#123;onDelete&#125;&gt;Delete project&lt;/<span class="t">Button</span>&gt;
      &lt;/<span class="t">Dialog.Content</span>&gt;
    &lt;/<span class="t">Dialog.Root</span>&gt;
  );
&#125;</code></pre><button class="copybtn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code to clipboard" title="Copy"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M19,21H8V7H19M19,5H8A2,2 0 0,0 6,7V21A2,2 0 0,0 8,23H19A2,2 0 0,0 21,21V7A2,2 0 0,0 19,5M16,1H4A2,2 0 0,0 2,3V17H4V3H16V1Z"/></svg></button></div>
      <div class="admonition admonition-tip"><div class="admonition-heading"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M6.5 0C3.48 0 1 2.19 1 5c0 .92.55 2.25 1 3 1.34 2.25 1.78 2.78 2 4v1h5v-1c.22-1.22.66-1.75 2-4 .45-.75 1-2.08 1-3 0-2.81-2.48-5-5.5-5zm3.64 7.48c-.25.44-.47.8-.67 1.11-.86 1.41-1.25 2.06-1.45 3.23-.02.05-.02.11-.02.17H5c0-.06 0-.13-.02-.17-.2-1.17-.59-1.83-1.45-3.23-.2-.31-.42-.67-.67-1.11C2.44 6.78 2 5.65 2 5c0-2.2 2.02-4 4.5-4 1.22 0 2.36.42 3.22 1.19C10.55 2.94 11 3.94 11 5c0 .66-.44 1.78-.86 2.48zM4 14h5c-.23 1.14-1.3 2-2.5 2s-2.27-.86-2.5-2z"/></svg><span>tip</span></div><div class="admonition-content"><p>The confirm button repeats the verb from the title: "Delete project", not "OK" or "Yes". People who skim the buttons still know what will happen.</p></div></div>

      <h2 id="focus">Focus management<a class="hash-link" href="#focus" aria-label="Direct link to Focus management">​</a></h2>
      <h3>Initial focus</h3>
      <p>By default, focus moves to the first focusable element inside the dialog. For destructive confirmations, start on the safe action instead, so an accidental Enter cancels rather than deletes.</p>
      <div class="codeblock"><pre><code><span class="k">const</span> cancelRef = <span class="f">useRef</span>(<span class="k">null</span>);

&lt;<span class="t">Dialog.Content</span> <span class="a">initialFocus</span>=&#123;cancelRef&#125;&gt;
  <span class="c">&#123;/* Destructive dialogs start on the safe action */&#125;</span>
  &lt;<span class="t">Dialog.Close</span> <span class="a">asChild</span>&gt;
    &lt;<span class="t">Button</span> <span class="a">ref</span>=&#123;cancelRef&#125;&gt;Cancel&lt;/<span class="t">Button</span>&gt;
  &lt;/<span class="t">Dialog.Close</span>&gt;
&lt;/<span class="t">Dialog.Content</span>&gt;</code></pre><button class="copybtn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code to clipboard" title="Copy"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M19,21H8V7H19M19,5H8A2,2 0 0,0 6,7V21A2,2 0 0,0 8,23H19A2,2 0 0,0 21,21V7A2,2 0 0,0 19,5M16,1H4A2,2 0 0,0 2,3V17H4V3H16V1Z"/></svg></button></div>
      <div class="admonition admonition-info"><div class="admonition-heading"><svg viewBox="0 0 14 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M6.3 5.69a.942.942 0 0 1-.28-.7c0-.28.09-.52.28-.7.19-.18.42-.28.7-.28.28 0 .52.09.7.28.18.19.28.42.28.7 0 .28-.09.52-.28.7a1 1 0 0 1-.7.3c-.28 0-.52-.11-.7-.3zM8 7.99c-.02-.25-.11-.48-.31-.69-.2-.19-.42-.3-.69-.31H6c-.27.02-.48.13-.69.31-.2.2-.3.44-.31.69h1v3c.02.27.11.5.31.69.2.2.42.31.69.31h1c.27 0 .48-.11.69-.31.2-.19.3-.42.31-.69H8V7.98v.01zM7 2.3c-3.14 0-5.7 2.54-5.7 5.68 0 3.14 2.56 5.7 5.7 5.7s5.7-2.55 5.7-5.7c0-3.15-2.56-5.69-5.7-5.69v.01zM7 .98c3.86 0 7 3.14 7 7s-3.14 7-7 7-7-3.12-7-7 3.14-7 7-7z"/></svg><span>info</span></div><div class="admonition-content"><p>Focus is trapped automatically while the dialog is open.</p></div></div>
      <h3>Returning focus</h3>
      <p>When the dialog closes, focus goes back to the element that opened it. If that element no longer exists, because the row was just deleted, pass <code>returnFocus=&#123;listRef&#125;</code> so keyboard users land somewhere sensible instead of the top of the page.</p>

      <h2 id="closing">Closing behavior<a class="hash-link" href="#closing" aria-label="Direct link to Closing behavior">​</a></h2>
      <p>Every dialog closes three ways: the Esc key, a visible close or cancel button, and, by default, a click on the backdrop. All three call <code>onOpenChange(false)</code>, so you handle closing in one place.</p>
      <div class="admonition admonition-warning"><div class="admonition-heading"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M8.893 1.5c-.183-.31-.52-.5-.887-.5s-.703.19-.886.5L.138 13.499a.98.98 0 0 0 0 1.001c.193.31.53.501.886.501h13.964c.367 0 .704-.19.877-.5a1.03 1.03 0 0 0 .01-1.002L8.893 1.5zm.133 11.497H6.987v-2.003h2.039v2.003zm0-3.004H6.987V5.987h2.039v4.006z"/></svg><span>warning</span></div><div class="admonition-content"><p>A stray click outside a half-filled form throws away the person's work. Set <code>closeOnBackdrop=&#123;false&#125;</code> for forms and destructive actions; Esc and the Cancel button still work.</p></div></div>
      <div class="admonition admonition-danger"><div class="admonition-heading"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.05.31c.81 2.17.41 3.38-.52 4.31C3.55 5.67 1.98 6.45.9 7.98c-1.45 2.05-1.7 6.53 3.53 7.7-2.2-1.16-2.67-4.52-.3-6.61-.61 2.03.53 3.33 1.94 2.86 1.39-.47 2.3.53 2.27 1.67-.02.78-.31 1.44-1.13 1.81 3.42-.59 4.78-3.42 4.78-5.56 0-2.84-2.53-3.22-1.25-5.61-1.52.13-2.03 1.13-1.89 2.75.09 1.08-1.02 1.8-1.86 1.33-.67-.41-.66-1.19-.06-1.78C8.18 5.31 8.68 2.45 5.05.32L5.03.3l.02.01z"/></svg><span>danger</span></div><div class="admonition-content"><p>Never disable Esc permanently!</p></div></div>

      <h2 id="motion">Motion<a class="hash-link" href="#motion" aria-label="Direct link to Motion">​</a></h2>
      <p>The dialog fades and scales from 96% over 220ms with an ease-out curve, and the backdrop fades on the same timing so they read as one surface. It stays centered rather than growing from the trigger. Under prefers-reduced-motion, the scale is dropped and only the fade remains.</p>
      <div class="codeblock"><pre><code><span class="c">/* What Dialog.Content ships with: enter in 220ms, centered */</span>
<span class="t">dialog</span> &#123;
  <span class="a">opacity</span>: 0;
  <span class="a">transform</span>: <span class="f">scale</span>(0.96);
  <span class="a">transition</span>: opacity 220ms var(--grain-ease-out),
              transform 220ms var(--grain-ease-out);
&#125;
<span class="t">dialog[open]</span> &#123; <span class="a">opacity</span>: 1; <span class="a">transform</span>: none; &#125;
<span class="k">@starting-style</span> &#123;
  <span class="t">dialog[open]</span> &#123; <span class="a">opacity</span>: 0; <span class="a">transform</span>: <span class="f">scale</span>(0.96); &#125;
&#125;</code></pre><button class="copybtn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code to clipboard" title="Copy"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M19,21H8V7H19M19,5H8A2,2 0 0,0 6,7V21A2,2 0 0,0 8,23H19A2,2 0 0,0 21,21V7A2,2 0 0,0 19,5M16,1H4A2,2 0 0,0 2,3V17H4V3H16V1Z"/></svg></button></div>
      <div class="admonition admonition-note"><div class="admonition-heading"><svg viewBox="0 0 14 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M6.3 5.69a.942.942 0 0 1-.28-.7c0-.28.09-.52.28-.7.19-.18.42-.28.7-.28.28 0 .52.09.7.28.18.19.28.42.28.7 0 .28-.09.52-.28.7a1 1 0 0 1-.7.3c-.28 0-.52-.11-.7-.3zM8 7.99c-.02-.25-.11-.48-.31-.69-.2-.19-.42-.3-.69-.31H6c-.27.02-.48.13-.69.31-.2.2-.3.44-.31.69h1v3c.02.27.11.5.31.69.2.2.42.31.69.31h1c.27 0 .48-.11.69-.31.2-.19.3-.42.31-.69H8V7.98v.01zM7 2.3c-3.14 0-5.7 2.54-5.7 5.68 0 3.14 2.56 5.7 5.7 5.7s5.7-2.55 5.7-5.7c0-3.15-2.56-5.69-5.7-5.69v.01zM7 .98c3.86 0 7 3.14 7 7s-3.14 7-7 7-7-3.12-7-7 3.14-7 7-7z"/></svg><span>note</span></div><div class="admonition-content"><p>Motion tokens are documented on the Motion page.</p></div></div>

      <h2 id="props">Props<a class="hash-link" href="#props" aria-label="Direct link to Props">​</a></h2>
      <p>Props for <code>Dialog.Content</code>. <code>Dialog.Root</code> accepts <code>open</code>, <code>defaultOpen</code>, and <code>onOpenChange</code>.</p>
      <table>
        <thead>
        <tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>modal</td><td>boolean</td><td>true</td><td>When false, renders a non-modal dialog that doesn't trap focus or block the page.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>initialFocus</td><td>RefObject</td><td>First focusable</td><td>Element that receives focus when the dialog opens.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>returnFocus</td><td>boolean | RefObject</td><td>true</td><td>Where focus goes on close. true means the trigger.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>closeOnBackdrop</td><td>boolean</td><td>true</td><td>Set to false for forms and destructive confirmations.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>closeOnEsc</td><td>boolean</td><td>true</td><td>Leave this on. Only disable it while a save is in flight.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>

      <h2 id="checklist">Accessibility checklist ✅<a class="hash-link" href="#checklist" aria-label="Direct link to Accessibility checklist ✅">​</a></h2>
      <p>✅ The dialog has a visible title, wired to aria-labelledby.<br />✅ Focus moves into the dialog on open and returns on close.<br />✅ Tab and Shift + Tab stay inside while it's open.<br />✅ Esc closes it, except while a save is in flight.<br />✅ Buttons name their action; the destructive one uses the danger variant.<br />✅ Content behind the dialog is inert to pointer, keyboard, and screen readers.</p>

